**AC-SN-25 (auto)**: GIVEN the D.1 fixture: ring-1 home body (`aboard` false, so `E1 = RING_EXPOSURE[1] = 0` at every level, whatever the floor), phase CALM and tier 0 (`E2` 0), `E4` 0, `crew_saner` false, `pending` 0, `startle_add` 0, `settled` forced false by a stubbed THIN `band_o2` (so `R = REC_IDLE` = 1 on every run), and the cap at 36; and GIVEN a scripted contact simulation of k horror stubs, each within 288 px: all k enter range together and stay until every `pay_h` is 0 (the contact phase), then all leave and stay out for exactly 600 runs (the gap; the 600th out-of-range run resets every `spent_h` to 0, D.10), and the cycle repeats WHEN it is driven until the first run whose `level'` is below 15000 THEN the 1-based count of whole runs from the start of the script to that run (the contact phase of cycle 1 starts at run 1) is exactly:
- k = 1 from 70000: run 18053 (cycle 25, contact run 53, `level'` 14993); the run before, 18052, ends at 15012;
- k = 1 from 43000: run 9053 (cycle 13, contact run 53, `level'` 14993); run 9052 ends at 15012;
- k = 2 from 43000: run 3917 (cycle 6, contact run 52, `level'` 14993);
- k = 3 from 43000: run 2816 (cycle 4, contact run 104, `level'` 14968);
- k = 4 from 43000: run 2050 (cycle 3, contact run 164, `level'` 14982).
Derivation, all at registry defaults (`EXP_HORROR` 20, `HORROR_ENC_BUDGET` 3000, `DRIFT_MAX_PER_RUN` 36, `REC_IDLE` 1; 'loss' = 70000 or 43000 minus level, and 'below 15000' means loss >= 55001 or >= 28001): k = 1: contact is 150 runs of `net` = 20 - 1 = 19 (2850 loss), the gap recovers 600, so a full 750-run cycle loses 2250. From 43000: 12 full cycles = 9000 runs, loss 27000; the 13th contact needs 19 x j >= 28001 - 27000 = 1001, j = 53 (1007; j = 52 gives 988); 9000 + 53 = 9053, level 43000 - 27000 - 1007 = 14993. From 70000: 24 full cycles = 18000 runs, loss 54000; 19 x j >= 55001 - 54000 = 1001, j = 53; 18053, level 70000 - 54000 - 1007 = 14993. k = 2: the cap binds (E3 40, `net` 36, charge `delta` = 36 - (-1) = 37 split in ascending ref order, 20 to horror 1 and 17 to horror 2) for 150 runs, then horror 2 alone (`net` 19, charge 20 per run, 450 left = 22 runs of 20 and one of 10): contact 173 runs, loss 5827, cycle 773 runs, net loss per cycle 5227. 5 cycles = 3865 runs, loss 26135; the 6th contact runs at `net` 36 and needs 36 x j >= 28001 - 26135 = 1866, j = 52; 3865 + 52 = 3917, level 43000 - 26135 - 1872 = 14993. k = 3: contact 304 runs (loss 8696), cycle 904, net 8096 per cycle; 3 cycles = 2712 runs, loss 24288; 36 x j >= 3713, j = 104; 2816, level 43000 - 24288 - 3744 = 14968. k = 4: contact 343 runs (loss 11657), cycle 943, net 11057; 2 cycles = 1886 runs, loss 22114; 36 x j >= 5887, j = 164; 2050, level 43000 - 22114 - 5904 = 14982. No 'about' and no 'at least': each count is asserted exactly in runs (never wall-clock; 9053 runs = 1810.6 s). The 'end of the Nth encounter' figures (13 x 150 + 12 x 600 = 9150 runs for k = 1) are not the first crossing and appear only in D.10 under that label. (D.1, D.10, EC-SN-19) *(Amended 2026-10-28 — delegated ruling G3/G4: oracle recomputed as the first run with level < 15000, E1 state stated.)*

